B.bb1=new A.j9("EB Garamond (Georg Duffner, Octavio Pardo), Literata (TypeTogether for Google) and Inter (Rasmus Andersson), all under the SIL Open Font License 1.1.",null)
B.bb2=new A.j9("Background paintings are photographic reproductions of public-domain works from Wikimedia Commons (commons.wikimedia.org), each marked public domain there:",null)
B.bb3=new A.j9("Liber et Libri is a free library of classic books with a focus (speed-reading) mode. Everything you read is stored only on this device. There are no accounts and no tracking.",null)
B.bb4=new A.j9("Speed-read mode shows one word at a time. It is great for focus and for getting through a chapter, but research shows that reading much faster usually costs some comprehension. Pick a pace that feels comfortable and switch back to the page whenever you like.",null)
B.bb5=new A.j9("Pride and Prejudice: plates by Hugh Thomson (George Allen, 1894) and C. E. Brock (Macmillan, 1895). Frankenstein: frontispiece and title-page vignette by Theodor von Holst, engraved by W. Chevalier (Colburn & Bentley, 1831). All are public domain; scans from Wikimedia Commons. Full per-plate sources are listed in the app\u2019s attribution file.",null)
B.bb6=new A.j9("The chapter-round and Crossword backdrops are open-access files released by the museums themselves:",null)
B.bb7=new A.j9("All books come from Standard Ebooks (standardebooks.org), a volunteer project that produces carefully proofread, beautifully formatted editions of public-domain works.",null)
B.bb8=new A.j9("Recordings are LibriVox (librivox.org) public-domain audiobooks read by volunteers, streamed from the Internet Archive (archive.org); each player names its reader. Read-along timing for a few pilot chapters was produced on our side by automatically aligning the recording with the text, so it can drift by a word or two. Liber et Libri is not affiliated with LibriVox or the Internet Archive.",null)
B.bb9=new A.j9("For reading in the app, the text has been converted to plain paragraphs; endnotes and some typographic details were left out.",null)
B.bba=new A.j9("Definitions come from Webster\u2019s Revised Unabridged Dictionary (G. & C. Merriam Co., 1913), a public-domain work, via the Project Gutenberg text (gutenberg.org/ebooks/29765) as parsed by the WebstersEnglishDictionary project on GitHub. It is used for tap-to-look-up in the reader; being from 1913, it reflects the usage and attitudes of its time. Vocabulary games and quizzes use our modern contextual definitions, based on Princeton WordNet 3.0 (\xa9 2006 Princeton University, WordNet License) and hand-checked.",null)
B.bbb=new A.j9("Standard Ebooks dedicates its editions (their formatting, proofreading and cover designs) to the public domain under the Creative Commons CC0 1.0 Universal Public Domain Dedication (creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/). The underlying texts are believed to be in the public domain in the United States; copyright status may differ in other countries. Liber et Libri is not affiliated with or endorsed by Standard Ebooks.",null)
B.bbc=new A.j9("In-app coin faces are photographic derivatives of Metropolitan Museum of Art Open Access coins (Rogers Fund, 1908), used under the Met Open Access / CC0 terms. Liber et Libri is not affiliated with or endorsed by the Metropolitan Museum of Art. Share cards credit coin imagery only as \u201cPublic domain\u201d.",null)
